Description: Context menus open on release, as on Windows
 GTK applications pop up a context menu from the press of the secondary
 button, and the menu then follows the X11 press-drag-release model: drag
 onto an item and let go to choose it. Windows takes two steps. The menu
 appears when the button is released and stays open until a second,
 separate click. Someone used to Windows lets go as soon as the menu
 appears and picks whatever item is under the pointer.
 .
 gtk_popover_popup() called while gtk_main_do_event() is dispatching a
 press of the secondary button now holds the popover back, and shows it
 once that button's release has been dispatched. Another press, a popdown
 or a drag starting from the press cancels it.
 .
 GtkModelButton also ignores unpaired releases of the secondary button.
 GtkGestureClick emits unpaired-release before its button filter runs, so
 the release of a right press that opened a menu by some other route would
 otherwise still choose the item under the pointer. Primary-button
 press-drag-release, which menu bars rely on and Windows also has, ordinary
 clicks and keyboard activation are unchanged.
Author: AltarsCN <altarscn2@gmail.com>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-10-03
---
--- a/gtk/gtkmodelbutton.c
+++ b/gtk/gtkmodelbutton.c
@@ -1533,6 +1533,17 @@ gesture_unpaired_release (GtkGestureClic
                           GdkEventSequence *sequence,
                           GtkWidget        *widget)
 {
+  /* An unpaired release is one whose press happened somewhere else.
+   * For the secondary button that is the press that opened this
+   * context menu, and choosing on its release is the X11
+   * press-drag-release model. Windows leaves the menu open and waits
+   * for a second, separate click, so ignore it. The primary button
+   * keeps press-drag-release, which menu bars rely on and Windows has
+   * too.
+   */
+  if (button == GDK_BUTTON_SECONDARY)
+    return;
+
   if (gtk_widget_contains (widget, x, y))
     g_signal_emit (widget, signals[SIGNAL_CLICKED], 0);
 }
